{"step_index":325,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-05T19:25:30Z","input_tokens":3045,"cache_read_tokens":61613,"output_tokens":1951,"thinking":"**Reviewing Command Structure**\n\nI'm currently dissecting the user's initial command, noting the preference for Option 2 (manual linking) in the first message. The subsequent message indicates a desire for both Option 1 and Option 2, but with an intervening step that I'll need to identify. I'm focusing on parsing the intent behind \"bb\" within this dual-option request.\n\n\n**Assessing Dual Execution & Status**\n\nI now understand the user's shift towards a combined approach – executing both the auto-installer and the manual documentation. Crucially, they want a status update beforehand, perfectly aligning with the `/plan` command's purpose. I will start by giving a status update on the PowerShell and UI fixes, and the established... I have established the current state and path to completion. I also decided I'll start by providing a status update. After that, I will also provide `install_theme.bat` for easy installation, *and* document the \"Requisito Previo\" in `README.md` with links to `docs/theme_dependency.md`.\n\n\n**Finalizing Documentation & Installer**\n\nI'm now fully immersed in the final polishing phase, ensuring everything aligns perfectly. I've finished documenting the PokeMMO Theme dependency in `docs/theme_dependency.md`, outlining the manual install steps. I've also completed the `scripts/install_theme.bat` installer script. It's designed for simple user experience, prompting for the PokeMMO path and handling the theme copy. I'm now just checking over everything before pushing.\n\n\n**Crafting a Status Update**\n\nI'm currently putting together a structured \"Bebita Table\" response as a status update. This includes greetings, a Japanese-inspired header (\"Joukyou\" for \"Current Status\"), and a table summarizing past work, outstanding items, and the planned hybrid approach. I'm focusing on clarity, emphasizing the completion of Ditto and PowerShell fixes, and clearly stating the combined approach of thorough documentation and the magic script. The `README.md` will list this as a prerequisite and the `install_theme.bat` will be provided for easy installation. I will then list the follow-up steps. I am confident that all code is robust and testable.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":true,"Summary":"Plan híbrido para manejar el tema mediante un instalador y documentación en el README","UserFacing":true},"CodeContent":"## Plan de Acción: Gestión Híbrida del Tema (Opción 1 + 2)\n\n### [Goal Description] (目的 - Mokuteki)\nImplementar una solución robusta y amigable para el problema de la dependencia estética del bot. Combinaremos la **Opción 1** (un script instalador) y la **Opción 2** (documentación como requisito previo estricto). De esta forma, explicamos *por qué* es obligatorio, pero damos la herramienta para resolverlo con un solo *click*.\n\n### Proposed Changes\n\n#### 1. [NEW] `docs/theme_dependency.md`\nCrearemos un documento exclusivo para explicar la dependencia visual.\n*   **Contenido:** Explicará que las coordenadas (OCR, HP, Menús) están fijadas a tu plantilla de PokéMMO actual. Si el tema cambia, el bot queda ciego.\n*   **Instrucciones Manuales:** Explicará cómo copiar la carpeta de `assets/pokemmo_theme` a `PokeMMO/data/themes` si el script falla.\n\n#### 2. [MODIFY] `README.md`\nAgregaremos una sección de **Requisitos Previos (Prerequisites)** muy clara.\n*   **Añadir:** \"⚠️ **Requisito Obligatorio:** El bot depende de un tema visual específico para PokéMMO. Lee la [Documentación de la Plantilla](docs/theme_dependency.md).\"\n*   **Añadir:** Instrucciones para ejecutar `scripts/install_theme.bat`.\n\n#### 3. [NEW] `scripts/install_theme.bat`\nUn script simple en *Batch* para automatizar el proceso sin marear al usuario.\n```bat\n@echo off\necho =